== Proton channel

At the reference setting, the p2 and p3 footprint centroids lie south and east of p1 (Fig. 3a,b). The signed differences (second minus first) are #val("ch_dlat_p2p1")#sq latitude and #val("ch_dlon_p2p1")#sq longitude for p2 − p1 (#val("ch_d_p2p1") km), #val("ch_dlat_p3p1")#sq and #val("ch_dlon_p3p1")#sq for p3 − p1 (#val("ch_d_p3p1") km), and #val("ch_dlat_p3p2")#sq and #val("ch_dlon_p3p2")#sq for p3 − p2 (#val("ch_d_p3p2") km). The footprints overlap substantially: the area-weighted Jaccard indices are #val("ch_jac_p2p1") (p1/p2), #val("ch_jac_p3p1") (p1/p3) and #val("ch_jac_p3p2") (p2/p3). For the top-10% footprint over both grids and statistics, the centroid distances between channels range from #val("ch_pd_min") to #val("ch_pd_max") km; other thresholds are listed in Supplement S4.

In paired calendar-block resampling, all 1,000 replicates were defined at every block length. The p3 − p1 latitude difference kept its sign throughout the central 95% of replicates: #val("bs_1_p3p1_lat_q025") to #val("bs_1_p3p1_lat_q975")#sq for 1-day blocks, #val("bs_3_p3p1_lat_q025") to #val("bs_3_p3p1_lat_q975")#sq for 3-day and #val("bs_7_p3p1_lat_q025") to #val("bs_7_p3p1_lat_q975")#sq for 7-day. The longitude difference ranged from #val("bs_1_p3p1_lon_q025") to #val("bs_1_p3p1_lon_q975")#sq, #val("bs_3_p3p1_lon_q025") to #val("bs_3_p3p1_lon_q975")#sq and #val("bs_7_p3p1_lon_q025") to #val("bs_7_p3p1_lon_q975")#sq. The p2 − p1 longitude range stays positive but approaches zero (#val("bs_1_p2p1_lon_q025") to #val("bs_1_p2p1_lon_q975")#sq for 1-day blocks). The p3 − p2 latitude range crosses zero at every block length (e.g. #val("bs_7_p3p2_lat_q025") to #val("bs_7_p3p2_lat_q975")#sq for 7-day blocks). Replicate medians are not identical to the observed differences, and widths change with block length; no block length was selected as preferred. These ranges describe the stability of the p1/p3 ordering under one month of day resampling. They do not remove the shared fitting assumptions linking the channels, the channels' different response functions, or calibration uncertainty.

The continuous normalized fields give a different summary (Fig. 3c). On the common eligible support, which is identical for the three channels (#val("cs_cells_5") cells at 5#sq, #val("cs_cells_2") at 2#sq), the p1/p3 mass overlap is #val("ch_ov_p3p1") and pairwise overlaps span #val("ch_ov_min")–#val("ch_ov_max") over both grids and statistics. The whole-field p1/p3 moment distance is #val("ch_cd_p3p1") km, compared with #val("ch_d_p3p1") km between footprint centroids. For p2/p3 the whole-field distance is only #val("ch_cd_p3p2") km, and its latitude difference changes sign (#val("ch_cdlat_p3p2")#sq, versus #val("ch_dlat_p3p2")#sq for the footprints). The choice of summary is therefore material: thresholding concentrates weight in the upper tail, and in this case the channels' fields differ most there. The #val("ch_cd_p3p1") km and #val("ch_d_p3p1") km figures summarize different statistics; their difference is not a causal threshold effect.

